      "answer": "- The train, test, and validation subsets in \"doclaynet.pdf\" are split at full-document boundaries, meaning that all pages from a single document are assigned to only one of the train, test, or validation sets and never split across them [1][2].\n- The authors chose this boundary to avoid having pages from the same document\u2014and therefore from the same unique layout\u2014in multiple sets, which could give models an unfair evaluation advantage and lead to overestimation of prediction accuracy if similar styles appear in both training and test sets [1][2].",
